<title>SOUTH KOREA: Korea Mobile changes company name.</title>
<headline>Korea Mobile changes company name.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-03-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Korea Mobile Telecom Co, South Korea's largest cellular phone and radio paging operator, said on Tuesday it had changed its name to SK Telecom Co Ltd.</p>
<p>The company said in a statement the change reflected its vision to grow into a provider of a wider range of telecommunications services.</p>
<p>The Sunkyong Group, the largest shareholder, has a 21.85 percent stake in the company. The state-run Korea Telecom holds an 18.99 percent stake and SEOULBANK an 11.39 percent, the statement said.</p>
<p>-- Seoul Newsroom (822) 727-5646</p>
</text>
